Source: libre-computer-archive-keyring
Priority: optional
Section: misc
Maintainer: Da Xue <da@libre.computer>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10)

Package: libre-computer-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: libretech-keyring (<< ${binary:Version})
Replaces: libretech-keyring (<< ${binary:Version})
Provides: libretech-keyring (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Libre Computer archive keyring
 The OpenPGP key that signs packages.libre.computer, at
 /usr/share/keyrings/libre-computer-deb.gpg (the path every source line names).
 .
 On a board still reading deb.libre.computer (the frozen repository) it moves the
 board's apt source to packages.libre.computer for its release, and once apt is
 free installs the libre-computer name of every package the board has under an
 old libretech name, removing nothing else. Kernel packages follow the owner's
 own upgrade. A release packages.libre.computer does not serve, a kernel channel
 other than lc-lts, or packages.libre.computer not answering keeps the board
 where it is.

Package: libretech-keyring
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
# Pre-Depends, not Depends: libre-computer-archive-keyring is unpacked first and takes the key, the scripts and
# the units over (Replaces), so unpacking this package never deletes them, even for a moment
Pre-Depends: libre-computer-archive-keyring (= ${binary:Version})
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: transitional package for libre-computer-archive-keyring
 The Libre Computer keyring is now libre-computer-archive-keyring. This
 package pulls it in and can be removed.
